    "q-67680": {
      "dom_id": "step-q67680",
      "name": "Question 2",
      "problem": "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14226856/assets/a8cd5ca7760d21ac5bd86cfb90486ccde755f4aba831808889a20e1ad467eaf9.png)\n\nFind the area of $△ABC.$ Round your answer to two decimal places.",
      "worked_solution": "The formula for the area of the triangle is \n\n$$\nA=\\frac{1}{2}ab\\operatorname{sin}⁡C,\n$$\n\nwhere $∠C$ is between the sides of lengths $a$ and $b.$ \n\nHere, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}b & =CA=8, \\\\ a & =CB=10, \\\\ m∠A & ={43}^{∘}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince \n\n$$\n\\operatorname{sin}⁡{43}^{∘}=0.681\\,998,\n$$\n\nrounded to six decimal places,  we calculate the area as follows:\n \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A & =\\frac{1}{2}\\cdot 10\\cdot 8\\cdot \\operatorname{sin}⁡{43}^{∘} \\\\  & =40\\cdot (0.681\\,998) \\\\  & ≈27.28\\,{\\text{cm}}^{2},\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nrounded to two decimal places.",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
